    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "MILLS ESTATE INCORPORATED\nMILLS BUILDING\nSAN FRANCISCO\nJanuary 28, 1927.\nJoseph J. Phillips dity and county of San Francisco,\nRight of Way Agent\nSan Francisco, California.\nDear Sir:\nMills Estate Incorporated is willing to lease to\nthe City and County of San Francisco, for use as a\ntemporary airport, one hundred and fiity (150) acres, or\nthereabouts,\nof its property at San Bruno heretofore\npointed out\nto you.\nThe terms of the lease acceptable\nto us are as follows:\nThe lease is to run for a period of three (3)\nvears at a rental oi len Dollars ($10) an acre per year.\nThis Ten Dollars (S10) per acre per year is arrivea at as\nfollows:\nThe value of the loss of the pasturage each year\nis estimated at Five Dollars ($5), and the maintenance\ncharges amount to Five Dollars ($5) a year.\nIn addition to the foregoing payments, we are to be\npaid the sum of Iwenty Five Dollars ($25) per\nacre at the\nend of the lease in order to recondition the land for the\npurposes for which it is now used. This reconditioning\ninvolves\nthe plowing, discing, harrowing and reseeding of\nthe property.\nWe shall maintain the levees during the term of the\nLease Just as we have maintained them in the past, but any\nlamages that may result from any breaking of the levees, or\nany other cause, must be borne by yourselves.\nWe understand that you desire to seed some parts\nif not all of the land in question, and if so such seeding\nas may be done must be with our consent in order that we may\nbe assured that no deleterious grasses will be grown on the\nproperty.\nAt the time being, we are maintaining and we shall\ncontinue\nthe maintenance of a pumping plant for use in\nconnection with this land. Any additional expenses over and\nabove those now borne by us for this pumping that may be\noccasioned because of your requirements, will be borne by\nyou•\nYou will be given permission to erect a water tank\non the adjacent property belonging to us, and to run a pipe\nline from that property to the land in question which you\nmay pipe as you see fit.",
      "Joseph J. Phillips, Esq.\nJanuary 28, 1927.\n-2-\nUpon the termination of the lease, you are to remove\nany and all structures and improvements erected by you and\nforeign substances hauled to the property, such as cinders,\ngravel, etc., to make it available for our uses. In making\nsuch removals you will be permitted to dump the waste in the\nold borrow pit or sloughs on the property in question.\nTrusting that the foregoing will be of assistance to\nyou in establishing your temporary airport, we are,\nVery truly yours,\nMILLS ESTATE INCORPORATED\nRight if way one the adjoining lal fo the caste dun.\nmante ane \u0026 semmel I fifeliet tanle.\nRialue A salioad:\nPinile jasiz dalmed lencert fiel mateñal.\nBater",
